MVP V0: Self-Improvement App — Refined Requirements
(Supersedes prior MVP v1 draft; based on DesignDocumentforV0.docx + mockups)

OVERVIEW
- Gamified daily task tracker: complete tasks tied to Mental/Physical growth → earn points → level up
- Single user (you), no login/auth needed

SCOPE
- 2 growth areas: Mental, Physical, plus a General tag for tasks not tied to either
- 2 screens only: Daily Tasks, Task Creation
- Very simple UI/leveling system

SCREEN 1: DAILY TASKS
- To-do list styled like iOS Reminders
- Each row: checkbox, task name, tag (Mental/Physical/General), points value
- "+" button opens Task Creation screen
- Progress bar at bottom showing progress toward next level
- Hidden dev/test button, bottom-left corner: resets level progress to 0 (for testing only, not user-facing)

SCREEN 2: TASK CREATION
- Fields: Task name (text)
- Date toggle + Time toggle (iOS Reminders style) — when on, a date/time picker appears, controlling when the task becomes visible/active on the Daily Tasks screen
- Repeat: dropdown, "Daily" only for V0 (no weekly/custom yet)
- End repeat: dropdown, e.g. "Never" (applies only if Repeat = Daily)
- Tag: single-select — Physical / Mental / General
- Points: dropdown of preset values (e.g. 1–10), any tag (including General) can carry points
- "Create task" button

POINTS & LEVELING
- Completing a task awards its point value once per day (recurring tasks re-award on each new day they're checked off)
- Leveling uses an increasing threshold per level (each level requires more points than the last)
  - Open question: exact formula (e.g. Level N needs N × 100, or exponential curve) — needs a number to lock in
- Dev/test mode lets you reset level/points to 0 to test the curve

OUT OF SCOPE FOR V0 (deferred)
- Multiple users / login
- More growth areas (Financial, Spiritual, Professional)
- Repeat frequencies other than Daily (weekly, custom)
- Editing/deleting existing tasks (not mentioned in design doc — confirm if needed)
- Notifications/reminders, streaks, bar-graph score model from earlier drafts

ARCHITECTURE RECOMMENDATION (brief, for future scaling)
- Client: cross-platform framework (React Native or Flutter) so V0 UI can later scale to more screens/areas without a rewrite
- Storage: local on-device DB (SQLite) for V0 single-user simplicity; design schema (tasks, tags, points, levels) so it can migrate to a backend later
- Structure growth areas/tags as config-driven data, not hardcoded, so adding Financial/Spiritual/Professional later is a data change, not a code change
- Keep leveling/points logic in a separate module (not tied to UI) so the formula can be tuned or moved server-side later
- Defer accounts/auth/cloud sync to v2, but avoid schema decisions now that would block adding a `user_id` later

OPEN QUESTIONS
- Exact points-to-level formula/curve
- Can tasks be edited or deleted after creation, or only created?
- Timezone/day-boundary rule for when a "new day" resets recurring tasks
- Preset points range — confirm 1–10 is the right ceiling

SIMILAR APPS (reference only)
- Habitica, Todoist (task checklist + points/gamification)
- iOS Reminders (list/UI style reference)
